1
00:00:00,125 --> 00:00:00,965
The first thing she did

2
00:00:00,965 --> 00:00:01,949
was to call me

3
00:00:01,949 --> 00:00:04,688
and thank me for the contribution

4
00:00:04,688 --> 00:00:05,639
I had in her life.

5
00:00:05,729 --> 00:00:06,709
Hi, I'm Syaheer.

6
00:00:06,709 --> 00:00:08,629
I've been a MENDAKI Achievement Programme (MAP) Coach

7
00:00:08,629 --> 00:00:10,069
since 2011,

8
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:11,144
which is about 15 years ago.

9
00:00:11,244 --> 00:00:13,223
Hi, I'm Nur Azyyati.

10
00:00:13,223 --> 00:00:15,315
Teaching has always been my passion.

11
00:00:15,425 --> 00:00:16,645
I used to be an educator,

12
00:00:16,645 --> 00:00:19,325
so I've moved out to IT

13
00:00:19,325 --> 00:00:20,452
in corporate roles.

14
00:00:20,452 --> 00:00:22,652
And this is my way of giving back

15
00:00:22,652 --> 00:00:25,436
and continuing my journey

16
00:00:25,436 --> 00:00:27,602
in contributing to the community

17
00:00:27,602 --> 00:00:28,362
in education.

18
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:30,107
I want to help those, especially students

19
00:00:30,107 --> 00:00:32,766
who need more guidance and support.

20
00:00:32,871 --> 00:00:35,131
I get to interact with a lot of students

21
00:00:35,131 --> 00:00:37,396
and I've touched many lives.

22
00:00:37,396 --> 00:00:38,876
When I meet them outside now,

23
00:00:38,876 --> 00:00:40,207
they are doing well.

24
00:00:40,207 --> 00:00:41,892
Before this, they were actually

25
00:00:41,892 --> 00:00:45,445
not very confident about themselves.

26
00:00:45,495 --> 00:00:47,255
It's fulfilling to see students

27
00:00:47,255 --> 00:00:49,575
who initially struggle,

28
00:00:49,575 --> 00:00:51,259
doubt themselves or lack motivation

29
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:52,339
slowly begin to believe

30
00:00:52,339 --> 00:00:53,387
in their own abilities.

31
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:55,422
Back in 2024, I was teaching

32
00:00:55,422 --> 00:00:56,960
a Primary 6 Foundation student.

33
00:00:56,960 --> 00:00:58,458
She has to retake her PSLE.

34
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:00,253
She worked really, really hard.

35
00:01:00,253 --> 00:01:01,094
She actually passed

36
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:02,631
her Math Foundation.

37
00:01:02,631 --> 00:01:04,151
I hope my students walk away

38
00:01:04,151 --> 00:01:06,171
with greater confidence in themselves

39
00:01:06,171 --> 00:01:07,611
and believe that they are capable

40
00:01:07,611 --> 00:01:09,570
of achieving more than they think.

41
00:01:09,630 --> 00:01:11,959
Our head coaches and coaches

42
00:01:11,959 --> 00:01:13,620
come from many different backgrounds,

43
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:14,942
not strictly just education.

44
00:01:14,977 --> 00:01:16,984
You don't have to be a perfect educator.

45
00:01:16,984 --> 00:01:18,984
As long as you are passionate,

46
00:01:18,984 --> 00:01:19,624
you have the patience

47
00:01:19,624 --> 00:01:21,644
and you are willing to have

48
00:01:21,644 --> 00:01:23,083
an impact on a child's life.

49
00:01:23,113 --> 00:01:24,748
If you are already thinking about it,

50
00:01:24,748 --> 00:01:25,469
sign up.
